<article class="env-lemma" id="07SA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07SA">Lemma <span data-tag="07SA">68.8.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be a quasi-compact, reasonable algebraic space over $S$. There exist an integer $n$ and open subspaces </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \emptyset = U_{n + 1} \subset U_ n \subset U_{n - 1} \subset \ldots \subset U_1 = X  \]
</div>
  <p> such that each $T_ p = U_ p \setminus U_{p + 1}$ (with reduced induced subspace structure) is a scheme. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate consequence of Lemma <a href="/tag/07S9" data-tag="07S9">68.8.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>